<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Old Quarter by Motorbike: Motorbike Rental Planning in Hanoi</h1>
<p>The Old Quarter is the dense, lively heart of Hanoi that most visitors come to see, and it is also the part of the city where a motorbike is both the most useful and the most demanding tool. The honest starting point for planning is geography: Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu operates from one verified location at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, across the Red River from the Old Quarter, not inside it. This page plans the rental around that fact honestly, from choosing the right machine for the Old Quarter's narrow lanes to bridging the river, finding parking without inventing rules, and matching the rental period to the days the plan actually contains.</p>
<p>We cover what the Long Bien pickup means for an Old Quarter plan, which verified fleet machines suit the area, how to approach the ride between the two neighbourhoods, how to ride and park inside the Old Quarter cautiously, and how to structure the rental period around verified prices. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the full fleet at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and browse wider riding advice in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>.</p>
